Repository guidance (generated by skillpack):

# fd-find

`fd` is a program to find entries in your filesystem. It is a simple, fast and user-friendly alternative to [`find`](https://www.gnu.org/software/findutils/). While it does not aim to support all of `find`'s powerful functionality, it provides sensible (opinionated) defaults for a majority of use cases.

## When to use

Invoke this tool when the user's task matches any of these triggers:

- `fd` is a program to find entries in your filesystem. It is a simple, fast and user-friendly alternative to [`find`](https://www.gnu.org/software/findutils/). While it does not aim to support all of `find`'s powerful functionality, it provides sensible (opinionated) defaults for a majority of use cases.


## When NOT to use

- Do not use this tool if the user only wants to *read* or *inspect* fd-find without performing an action — prefer reading docs directly.
- Do not use this tool for tasks outside the Rust tooling it was built for.

## Installation

Ensure `fd` is installed and available on PATH before invoking the examples below.

## Invocation

The exact command an agent should run to use this tool:

```
fd
```

